    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1205">

                <pb facs="0852" n="736" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg736"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.512/211.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Consul Hostetter.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of Stater</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-03-16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 16, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Consul, Mazatlan, reports that Constitutionalist authorities are collecting from
                    American mining companies back taxes which have already been paid to central
                    administration.</p>
                <p>Bring to attention of appropriate authorities with protest against collection
                    these taxes a second time, and state that under principles of international law
                    these companies should be relieved of all further obligation with regard to
                    taxes already paid by them to central administration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
